### Preflight Checklist

- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.
- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.
- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.

### Electron Version

39.0.0-beta.1, 38.2.2, 33.0.2

### What operating system(s) are you using?

Windows

### Operating System Version

Windows 10 Pro

### What arch are you using?

x64

### Last Known Working Electron version

33.0.2

### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?

Yes

### Expected Behavior

The user should be able to share either the audio from a specific browser tab or the system audio, depending on their selection when initiating screen sharing.

### Actual Behavior

When we include audio track that we got in Electron screen sharing, the receiver hears both the tab audio and a loopback of the receivers audio, causing echo.
Capturing tab audio only without echo is not working with the current getUserMedia/desktopCapturer approach.

### Testcase Gist URL

https://gist.github.com/MimikFc7/1632e2d54c420434450b7353f16b8114

### Additional Information

constraints = {
			audio: {
				mandatory: {
					echoCancellation: true,
					chromeMediaSource: 'desktop',
					chromeMediaSourceId: sourceId
				}
			} as any,
			video: {
				mandatory: {
					chromeMediaSource: 'desktop',
					chromeMediaSourceId: sourceId
				}
			} as any
		};
stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia(constraints);

